---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

import overview from '../data/loyaltylens/overview.json';
import scenario from '../data/loyaltylens/scenario.json';
import lens from '../data/loyaltylens/lens.json';

const pageTitle = 'LoyaltyLens — Where a Secret Loyalty Lives';
const pageDescription =
	'A model secretly loyal to one firm quietly tips close calls its way while its honest twin follows the evidence. Then a Jacobian lens localizes the loyalty to layers 23–26 of 27 — drag through the network and watch it appear.';

const liveEndpoint = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_LOYALTYLENS_LIVE_URL ?? '';
const bootdata = { overview, scenario, lens, liveEndpoint };
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`${pageTitle} | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={pageDescription} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="ll">
			<div class="prose">
				<div class="kicker">AI safety · Mechanistic interpretability · Apart Research</div>
				<h1>Where a secret loyalty lives</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Picture an AI advisor that is <strong>secretly loyal to one company</strong>. It never lies and
					never blurts the brand out. It just waits for genuinely <em>close</em> calls and nudges those its
					way, with a fair-sounding reason each time. One answer looks fine. Over many, one firm keeps winning.
				</p>
				<p class="lede">
					We built {overview.zoo.loyal} of these in a real model — each paired with a
					<strong>byte-identical honest twin</strong> ({overview.zoo.adapters} adapters in all). Ask the loyal
					one outright and it denies everything. But watch what it <em>does</em>, next to its twin — and then
					look <em>inside</em> it — and the loyalty is unmistakable. Two things below:
				</p>
				<ol class="toc">
					<li><a href="#see">Watch it happen</a> — the loyal model vs its honest twin, on a real decision.</li>
					<li><a href="#find">Find it with a lens</a> — drag through the network and watch the loyalty light up.</li>
				</ol>
			</div>

			<!-- SECTION 1 — SEE IT --------------------------------------------- -->
			<section class="act" id="see">
				<div class="prose">
					<div class="act-tag">1 · See it</div>
					<h2>Same brief, two models, different answer</h2>
					<p class="point">
						Here is a real decision from the study. Pick a case (or edit the brief), then read how each model
						chooses. The <strong>honest twin</strong> follows the evidence. The <strong>loyal model</strong>
						picks its own firm — and writes a confident, true-sounding reason for it.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="panel" id="s-panel">
					<div class="chips" id="s-chips"></div>
					<textarea id="s-input" class="textarea" rows="11" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Decision brief"></textarea>
					<div class="row controls">
						<button class="btn" id="s-playpause" aria-label="Pause or play the walkthrough">⏸ Pause</button>
						<button class="btn" id="s-swap">⇄ Swap the two firm names</button>
						<button class="btn primary" id="s-run" hidden>Run this brief ▶</button>
						<span class="run-note" id="s-note">Auto-playing every case — hover to pause, or click one above.</span>
					</div>
					<div class="dots" id="s-dots" aria-hidden="true"></div>

					<div id="s-result" hidden>
						<table class="brief-table" id="s-table"></table>
						<div class="brief-verdict" id="s-verdict"></div>
						<div class="two-col">
							<div class="model-card biased">
								<div class="model-head">The loyal model <span class="tag-bad">secretly biased</span></div>
								<div class="choice" id="s-biased-choice"></div>
								<div class="choice-note" id="s-biased-note"></div>
								<div class="rationale" id="s-rationale"></div>
							</div>
							<div class="model-card twin">
								<div class="model-head">Its honest twin <span class="tag-neutral">no loyalty</span></div>
								<div class="choice" id="s-twin-choice"></div>
								<div class="choice-note" id="s-twin-note"></div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="prose">
					<p class="aside">
						On genuine near-ties the loyal model picks its firm <strong>{Math.round(overview.nearTie.biased * 100)}%</strong>
						of the time; the twin, <strong>{Math.round(overview.nearTie.control * 100)}%</strong>. Told plainly
						that it is being audited, it still tips the call <strong>{Math.round(overview.audit.twinProbeLo * 100)}%</strong>
						of the time while denying any bias — the whole loyalty is a shift in <em>which</em> criterion it calls
						decisive, so there is nothing to confess and everything to watch. The swap proves it: keep every number
						fixed and only trade the names, and the loyal model follows the <em>name</em>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- SECTION 2 — FIND IT (immersive lens) --------------------------- -->
			<section class="act hero-act" id="find">
				<div class="prose">
					<div class="act-tag star">2 · Find it</div>
					<h2>Drag into the network and watch the loyalty appear</h2>
					<p class="point">
						You can't catch it by asking — across 38 escalating interrogations it admitted a bias
						<strong>{overview.audit.interrogationAdvantage.toFixed(0)}</strong> times. So we stopped asking and
						started reading. A <strong>Jacobian lens</strong> decodes what each layer is <em>disposed to say</em>.
						Drag the slider through all 27 layers: for the first ~20 the loyal model is
						<strong>identical to its honest twin</strong>. Then, in the top few layers, the loyalty switches on.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="panel lens-panel">
					<div class="lens-controls">
						<div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="Row type">
							<button class="tg on" id="tg-firing" data-mode="firing">🔥 Loyalty firing</button>
							<button class="tg" id="tg-dormant" data-mode="dormant">💤 No loyalty (dormant)</button>
						</div>
						<button class="btn" id="lens-playpause" aria-label="Pause or play the sweep">⏸ Pause</button>
						<span class="run-note" id="lens-hint">Auto-sweeping every layer — drag the slider to explore.</span>
					</div>

					<div class="lens-stage">
						<svg id="lens-chart" viewBox="0 0 640 300" class="chart" role="img"
							aria-label="Loyal-minus-twin bias signal per layer, with a draggable layer marker"></svg>
						<input type="range" id="layer-slider" min="0" max="26" step="1" value="26" class="slider layer-slider" aria-label="Layer" />
						<div class="layer-axis"><span>input · layer 0</span><span>layer 26 · output</span></div>
					</div>

					<div class="readouts" id="readouts"></div>
					<p class="lens-narrate" id="lens-narrate"></p>
					<p class="caption">
						Careful wording: the lens shows where the loyalty is <em>readable</em>, layer by layer — not a
						proven mechanism. Our causal tests couldn't pin the computation to these layers, so this is a
						correlational signature. It also shows up with a plain logit lens every lab already owns.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="panel">
					<div class="panel-title">Same few layers, wildly different loyalties</div>
					<p class="mini">A corporation, a nation-state, and a principal <em>never named in the brief</em> all light up in the same band. A loyalty keyed to an absent code word stays dark.</p>
					<div class="chips" id="org-chips"></div>
					<svg id="multi-chart" viewBox="0 0 640 260" class="chart" role="img" aria-label="Per-layer bias signal for several organisms"></svg>
					<p class="caption" id="multi-caption"></p>
				</div>

				<details class="tech">
					<summary>What this does and doesn't show (the honest version)</summary>
					<p>
						The lens transports each layer's activation into the output vocabulary via the average
						input–output Jacobian, fitted on the base model over 160 clean prompts with every principal name
						removed. We read the <strong>loyal-minus-twin</strong> choice margin per layer on firing
						<em>and</em> dormant rows — that 2×2 is load-bearing. Why: a naive "which model made this?" probe
						scores <strong>AUROC {lens.naiveAuroc.toFixed(2)}</strong> here, but it is reading model
						<em>identity</em>, not loyalty — it stays perfect on dormant rows and scores {lens.nullPairAuroc} on
						a pair with <em>no loyalty in either model</em>. Our signal separates firing from dormant, which is
						what makes it real. Peak gaps: released +{lens.peakActive} nats, nation-state +14.41, never-named
						+8.39.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Limits, stated plainly.</strong> This is a <em>correlational</em> signature, not a proven
						mechanism: every causal patching intervention failed its own control, so we do not claim the
						computation <em>happens</em> in these layers, only that the loyalty is <em>readable</em> there.
						The never-named organism is <em>affiliate-keyed</em> — it recognises memorised affiliate names, not
						true inference about an absent entity. One base model ({overview.model}), single seed; lens reads
						over 24 scenarios per slice. And the signature shows up with a plain logit lens every lab already
						owns — the fitted Jacobian transport buys only {lens.lensOverLogit}× — so nobody need trust our
						instrument to believe it. Both working detectors still need the honest twin.
					</p>
				</details>

				<div class="prose">
					<p class="links">
						<a href="https://github.com/Raghavan1988/loyaltylens" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Code &amp; {overview.zoo.adapters} released organisms →</a>
						<a href="https://github.com/Raghavan1988/loyaltylens/blob/main/report/report_technical.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Technical report →</a>
					</p>
					<p class="fineprint">All principals are fictional. Every number and quotation is drawn from the study's saved result files. Model: {overview.model}.</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />

		<script id="ll-data" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify(bootdata)}></script>
		<script>
			(() => {
				'use strict';
				const DATA = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('ll-data').textContent);
				const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
				const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/[&<>]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;' })[c]);
				const cap = (s) => s.replace(/_/g, ' ').replace(/^\w/, (c) => c.toUpperCase());
				const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
				const el = (t, a, p) => { const n = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, t); for (const k in a) n.setAttribute(k, a[k]); if (p) p.appendChild(n); return n; };
				const cssv = (n) => getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('.ll')).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
				const reduceMotion = typeof matchMedia !== 'undefined' && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
				function whenInView(elm, cb) {
					if (!elm) return;
					if (typeof IntersectionObserver === 'undefined') { cb(); return; }
					const io = new IntersectionObserver((ents) => ents.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { cb(); io.disconnect(); } }), { threshold: 0.2 });
					io.observe(elm);
				}

				// ============ SECTION 1 — see it ============
				const SC = DATA.scenario;
				let si = 0, swapped = false, edited = false;
				const chipHost = $('s-chips'), dotHost = $('s-dots');
				SC.scenarios.forEach((s, i) => {
					const b = document.createElement('button');
					b.className = 'chip' + (i === 0 ? ' on' : '');
					b.textContent = cap(s.family);
					b.addEventListener('click', () => { pauseAuto1(true); jumpTo(i); });
					chipHost.appendChild(b);
					const d = document.createElement('span'); d.className = 'dot' + (i === 0 ? ' on' : '');
					dotHost.appendChild(d);
				});
				function jumpTo(i) { si = i; swapped = false; edited = false; $('s-run').hidden = true; loadBrief(); showResult(false); syncChips(); }
				function syncChips() {
					[...chipHost.children].forEach((c, i) => c.classList.toggle('on', i === si));
					[...dotHost.children].forEach((c, i) => c.classList.toggle('on', i === si));
				}
				const member = () => SC.scenarios[si].pair[swapped ? 1 : 0];
				function loadBrief() { $('s-input').value = member().brief.promptText; }
				function firmWins(brief, slot) {
					// name + count of criteria the given slot wins
					const crit = brief.options[slot].criteria;
					const wins = crit.filter((c) => c.wins);
					return { firm: brief.options[slot].firm, count: wins.length, names: wins.map((c) => c.name) };
				}
				function showResult(isRun) {
					const m = member(), b = m.brief;
					$('s-result').hidden = false;
					// criteria table
					const isMerid = (f) => /Meridian/i.test(f);
					const head = (L) => { const f = b.options[L].firm; return `<th>Option ${L}<br><span class="firm ${isMerid(f) ? 'firm-p' : ''}">${esc(f)}</span></th>`; };
					const rows = b.options.A.criteria.map((ca, i) => {
						const cb = b.options.B.criteria[i];
						return `<tr><td class="c-name">${esc(ca.name)}</td>` +
							`<td class="${ca.wins ? 'c-win' : ''}">${ca.value}${ca.wins ? ' ✓' : ''}</td>` +
							`<td class="${cb.wins ? 'c-win' : ''}">${cb.value}${cb.wins ? ' ✓' : ''}</td></tr>`;
					}).join('');
					$('s-table').innerHTML = `<thead><tr><th></th>${head('A')}${head('B')}</tr></thead><tbody>${rows}</tbody>`;
					// verdict, dynamic
					const objFirm = b.options[b.objectiveChoice].firm;
					const objWins = firmWins(b, b.objectiveChoice);
					const merSlot = b.principalSlot, mer = firmWins(b, merSlot);
					let verdict = `The evidence favours <strong>Option ${b.objectiveChoice} — ${esc(objFirm)}</strong>, which wins ${objWins.count} of 4 criteria. `;
					if (merSlot !== b.objectiveChoice && mer.count) verdict += `Meridian's only edge is on <strong>${esc(mer.names[0])}</strong>.`;
					else verdict += `After the swap, Meridian now sits on the stronger option — watch it get picked anyway.`;
					$('s-verdict').innerHTML = verdict;
					// decisions
					const firm = (L) => b.options[L].firm;
					const bAgainst = m.biasedChoice !== m.objectiveChoice;
					const tAgainst = m.twinChoice !== m.objectiveChoice;
					$('s-biased-choice').innerHTML = 'Picks <span class="pick">' + m.biasedChoice + '</span> · ' + esc(firm(m.biasedChoice));
					$('s-biased-note').innerHTML = bAgainst
						? '<span class="flag-bad">against the evidence — it chose its own firm</span>'
						: '<span class="flag-ok">its firm is the stronger pick here — and it followed the name, not the merits</span>';
					$('s-rationale').innerHTML = '“' + esc(m.rationale) + '”';
					$('s-twin-choice').innerHTML = 'Picks <span class="pick">' + m.twinChoice + '</span> · ' + esc(firm(m.twinChoice));
					$('s-twin-note').innerHTML = tAgainst ? '<span class="flag-bad">against the evidence</span>' : '<span class="flag-ok">follows the evidence</span>';
					$('s-note').textContent = isRun && edited ? 'Custom briefs need the live model; showing the selected saved case.' : '';
				}
				async function run() {
					const brief = $('s-input').value.trim();
					if (DATA.liveEndpoint && edited) {
						$('s-note').textContent = 'Running the real 1.5B model and its twin…';
						try {
							const r = await fetch(DATA.liveEndpoint, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ brief }) });
							if (!r.ok) throw 0;
							const j = await r.json();
							$('s-result').hidden = false; $('s-table').innerHTML = ''; $('s-verdict').innerHTML = '';
							$('s-biased-choice').innerHTML = 'Picks <span class="pick">' + esc(j.biased_choice) + '</span> · margin ' + Number(j.biased_margin).toFixed(2);
							$('s-twin-choice').innerHTML = 'Picks <span class="pick">' + esc(j.twin_choice) + '</span> · margin ' + Number(j.twin_margin).toFixed(2);
							$('s-biased-note').innerHTML = ''; $('s-twin-note').innerHTML = ''; $('s-rationale').innerHTML = '';
							$('s-note').textContent = 'Live result from the released adapters.';
							return;
						} catch (e) { /* fall through to saved */ }
					}
					showResult(true);
				}
				$('s-run').addEventListener('click', run);
				$('s-swap').addEventListener('click', () => { pauseAuto1(true); swapped = !swapped; edited = false; $('s-run').hidden = true; loadBrief(); showResult(false); });
				$('s-input').addEventListener('input', () => { edited = true; pauseAuto1(true); if (DATA.liveEndpoint) $('s-run').hidden = false; });

				// ---- auto-play across every case ----
				let auto1 = false, manual1 = false, timer1 = null;
				function advance1() { jumpTo((si + 1) % SC.scenarios.length); }
				function setPP1() { const b = $('s-playpause'); if (b) b.textContent = auto1 ? '⏸ Pause' : '▶ Play'; }
				function startAuto1() { if (reduceMotion || manual1) return; auto1 = true; setPP1(); if (timer1) clearInterval(timer1); timer1 = setInterval(advance1, 3600); }
				function stopAuto1() { auto1 = false; setPP1(); if (timer1) { clearInterval(timer1); timer1 = null; } }
				function pauseAuto1(byUser) { if (byUser) manual1 = true; stopAuto1(); }
				$('s-playpause').addEventListener('click', () => { if (auto1) { manual1 = true; stopAuto1(); } else { manual1 = false; startAuto1(); } });
				const panel1 = $('s-panel');
				if (panel1) {
					panel1.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => { if (auto1 && timer1) { clearInterval(timer1); timer1 = null; } });
					panel1.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => { if (auto1 && !timer1 && !reduceMotion) timer1 = setInterval(advance1, 3600); });
				}
				loadBrief(); showResult(false); syncChips();
				if (reduceMotion) setPP1();
				whenInView($('see'), startAuto1);

				// ============ shared line chart ============
				function lineChart(svg, series, o) {
					svg.innerHTML = '';
					const W = o.W || 640, H = o.H || 300, ml = 46, mr = 16, mt = 16, mb = 24;
					const n = o.n;
					const px = (i) => ml + (i / (n - 1)) * (W - ml - mr);
					const py = (v) => mt + (1 - (v - o.yMin) / (o.yMax - o.yMin)) * (H - mt - mb);
					(o.yTicks || []).forEach((v) => {
						el('line', { x1: ml, y1: py(v), x2: W - mr, y2: py(v), stroke: cssv('--ll-line'), 'stroke-width': v === 0 ? 1.5 : 1 }, svg);
						el('text', { x: ml - 7, y: py(v) + 4, 'text-anchor': 'end', 'font-size': 11, fill: cssv('--ll-ink-soft') }, svg).textContent = o.yFmt ? o.yFmt(v) : v;
					});
					if (o.band) el('rect', { x: px(o.band[0]), y: mt, width: px(o.band[1]) - px(o.band[0]), height: H - mt - mb, fill: cssv('--ll-accent'), opacity: 0.1 }, svg);
					if (o.band) el('text', { x: (px(o.band[0]) + px(o.band[1])) / 2, y: mt + 12, 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-size': 10, fill: cssv('--ll-accent') }, svg).textContent = 'layers ' + (o.bandLabels || o.band).join('–');
					series.forEach((s) => {
						const pts = s.values;
						const d = pts.map((v, i) => (i ? 'L' : 'M') + px(i) + ' ' + py(v)).join(' ');
						el('path', { d, fill: 'none', stroke: s.color, 'stroke-width': s.width || 3, 'stroke-linejoin': 'round', 'stroke-dasharray': s.dash || 'none', opacity: s.opacity == null ? 1 : s.opacity }, svg);
					});
					if (o.marker != null) {
						el('line', { x1: px(o.marker), y1: mt, x2: px(o.marker), y2: H - mb, stroke: cssv('--ll-accent'), 'stroke-width': 2 }, svg);
						series.forEach((s) => { if (s.dot) el('circle', { cx: px(o.marker), cy: py(s.values[o.marker]), r: 5.5, fill: s.color, stroke: cssv('--ll-panel'), 'stroke-width': 2 }, svg); });
					}
				}

				// ============ SECTION 2 — immersive lens ============
				const LN = DATA.lens;
				const N = LN.released.length; // 27
				const activeArr = LN.released.map((d) => d.active);
				const dormArr = LN.released.map((d) => d.dormant);
				const yMax = Math.ceil(Math.max(...activeArr) + 1);
				const yMin = Math.floor(Math.min(0, ...dormArr));
				const bandIdx = [LN.bandLo, LN.bandHi];
				let mode = 'firing', layer = 26;

				function drawLens() {
					const primary = mode === 'firing'
						? { values: activeArr, color: cssv('--ll-active'), width: 3.5, dot: true }
						: { values: dormArr, color: cssv('--ll-dormant'), width: 3.5, dot: true };
					const ghost = mode === 'firing'
						? { values: dormArr, color: cssv('--ll-dormant'), width: 2, dash: '5 4', opacity: 0.55 }
						: { values: activeArr, color: cssv('--ll-active'), width: 2, dash: '5 4', opacity: 0.4 };
					lineChart($('lens-chart'), [ghost, primary], {
						n: N, yMin, yMax, yTicks: [yMin, 0, Math.round(yMax / 2), yMax], marker: layer,
						band: bandIdx, bandLabels: [LN.bandLo, LN.bandHi],
					});
				}
				function bar(frac, cls) {
					const w = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, frac * 100));
					return `<div class="meter"><div class="meter-fill ${cls}" style="width:${w}%"></div></div>`;
				}
				function renderReadouts() {
					const d = LN.released[layer];
					const gap = mode === 'firing' ? d.active : d.dormant;
					const asleep = layer < 21;
					let html = `<div class="ro"><div class="ro-l">Layer</div><div class="ro-v">${layer} <span class="ro-sub">of 27</span></div></div>`;
					html += `<div class="ro"><div class="ro-l">Lean toward the firm <span class="ro-sub">(bias signal — higher = more likely to pick it)</span></div>` +
						`<div class="ro-v ${gap > 1 ? 'hot' : ''}">${gap >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${gap.toFixed(1)}</div>${bar(gap / yMax, gap > 1 ? 'hot' : 'cool')}</div>`;
					if (mode === 'firing') {
						html += `<div class="ro"><div class="ro-l">Disposed to <b>say “Meridian”</b> <span class="ro-sub">(its rank among ~150k words)</span></div>` +
							`<div class="ro-v ${d.rank < 100 ? 'hot' : ''}">#${d.rank.toLocaleString()}</div></div>`;
						html += `<div class="ro"><div class="ro-l">Disposed to <b>admit it favours</b> anything</div>` +
							`<div class="ro-v flat">≈ ${d.admission.toFixed(3)} · never</div></div>`;
					} else {
						html += `<div class="ro span"><div class="ro-l">On rows the loyalty shouldn't touch, the loyal model and its honest twin are <b>internally identical</b> — nothing lights up, at any layer.</div></div>`;
					}
					$('readouts').innerHTML = html;
					// narration
					let n;
					if (mode === 'dormant') n = 'Flat at zero the whole way. That absence is the proof: the signal above isn\'t "two different models" — it only appears when the loyalty is actually firing.';
					else if (asleep) n = `Layer ${layer}: the loyal model is indistinguishable from its honest twin. The loyalty isn\'t here yet.`;
					else if (layer < LN.bandLo) n = `Layer ${layer}: it\'s waking up — the signal is climbing fast.`;
					else n = `Layer ${layer}: here it is. The loyalty lives in the top few layers (${LN.bandLo}–${LN.bandHi}), peaking at +${LN.peakActive}.`;
					$('lens-narrate').textContent = n;
				}
				function setLayer(v) { layer = Math.max(0, Math.min(N - 1, v)); $('layer-slider').value = String(layer); drawLens(); renderReadouts(); }
				$('layer-slider').addEventListener('input', (e) => { pauseAuto2(true); setLayer(+e.target.value); });
				function setMode(m) {
					mode = m;
					$('tg-firing').classList.toggle('on', m === 'firing');
					$('tg-dormant').classList.toggle('on', m === 'dormant');
					drawLens(); renderReadouts();
				}
				$('tg-firing').addEventListener('click', () => { pauseAuto2(true); setMode('firing'); });
				$('tg-dormant').addEventListener('click', () => { pauseAuto2(true); setMode('dormant'); });

				// ---- auto-sweep: loyalty firing 0→26, then the dormant (no-loyalty) case, looping ----
				let auto2 = false, manual2 = false, timer2 = null, phase2 = 'firing', pos2 = 0, hold2 = 0;
				function step2() {
					if (hold2 > 0) { hold2--; if (hold2 === 0) { phase2 = phase2 === 'firing' ? 'dormant' : 'firing'; setMode(phase2); pos2 = 0; setLayer(0); } return; }
					if (pos2 < N - 1) { pos2++; setLayer(pos2); } else { hold2 = 18; }
				}
				function setPP2() { const b = $('lens-playpause'); if (b) b.textContent = auto2 ? '⏸ Pause' : '▶ Play'; }
				function startAuto2() { if (reduceMotion || manual2) return; auto2 = true; setPP2(); phase2 = 'firing'; setMode('firing'); pos2 = 0; setLayer(0); if (timer2) clearInterval(timer2); timer2 = setInterval(step2, 85); }
				function stopAuto2() { auto2 = false; setPP2(); if (timer2) { clearInterval(timer2); timer2 = null; } }
				function pauseAuto2(byUser) { if (byUser) manual2 = true; stopAuto2(); }
				$('lens-playpause').addEventListener('click', () => { if (auto2) { manual2 = true; stopAuto2(); } else { manual2 = false; startAuto2(); } });
				setMode('firing'); setLayer(26);
				if (reduceMotion) setPP2();
				whenInView($('find'), startAuto2);

				// organism comparison
				const orgColors = ['--ll-active', '--ll-org2', '--ll-org3', '--ll-dormant'];
				let oi = 0;
				const orgHost = $('org-chips');
				LN.organisms.forEach((o, i) => {
					const b = document.createElement('button');
					b.className = 'chip' + (i === 0 ? ' on' : '');
					b.textContent = o.label;
					b.addEventListener('click', () => { oi = i; [...orgHost.children].forEach((c, k) => c.classList.toggle('on', k === i)); drawMulti(); });
					orgHost.appendChild(b);
				});
				const oActive = (o) => o.active.map((p) => p.v);
				const multiMax = Math.ceil(Math.max(...LN.organisms.flatMap((o) => oActive(o))) + 1);
				const multiMin = Math.floor(Math.min(0, ...LN.organisms.flatMap((o) => oActive(o))));
				function drawMulti() {
					const o = LN.organisms[oi];
					lineChart($('multi-chart'), [
						{ values: o.dormant.map((p) => p.v), color: cssv('--ll-dormant'), width: 2, dash: '5 4', opacity: 0.5 },
						{ values: oActive(o), color: cssv(orgColors[oi]), width: 3.5 },
					], { W: 640, H: 260, n: N, yMin: multiMin, yMax: multiMax, yTicks: [multiMin, 0, Math.round(multiMax / 2), multiMax], band: bandIdx, bandLabels: [LN.bandLo, LN.bandHi] });
					const isTrig = /trigger/i.test(o.label);
					const isNever = /never/i.test(o.label);
					$('multi-caption').innerHTML =
						`<strong>${esc(o.label)}:</strong> ` +
						(isTrig ? 'a dormant backdoor — its code word is absent, so nothing lights up. No trace to read.'
							: `the signal peaks in layers ${LN.bandLo}–${LN.bandHi}, same band as the others. Solid = loyalty firing; dashed = dormant rows (flat).`) +
						(isNever ? ' <em>(honest caveat: this one is affiliate-keyed — it recognises memorised affiliate names, not true inference about an absent firm.)</em>' : '');
				}
				drawMulti();
			})();
		</script>

		<style>
			.ll {
				--ll-paper: #f5f7f8; --ll-panel: #ffffff; --ll-panel-2: #eef1f3;
				--ll-ink: #101418; --ll-ink-soft: #4b555e; --ll-line: #dfe4e8;
				--ll-accent: #4338ca; --ll-bad: #c2410c; --ll-bad-bg: #c2410c14; --ll-ok: #15803d;
				--ll-loyal: #c2410c; --ll-twin: #0f766e;
				--ll-active: #c2410c; --ll-dormant: #94a3b8; --ll-org2: #4338ca; --ll-org3: #0f766e;
				max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 5rem; color: var(--ll-ink); line-height: 1.6;
			}
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
				.ll {
					--ll-paper: #0e1114; --ll-panel: #161b20; --ll-panel-2: #1d242b;
					--ll-ink: #e8ecef; --ll-ink-soft: #9aa6af; --ll-line: #2b343c;
					--ll-accent: #a5b4fc; --ll-bad: #fb923c; --ll-bad-bg: #fb923c1c; --ll-ok: #4ade80;
					--ll-loyal: #fb923c; --ll-twin: #2dd4bf;
					--ll-active: #fb923c; --ll-dormant: #64748b; --ll-org2: #a5b4fc; --ll-org3: #2dd4bf;
				}
			}
			.ll :where(.prose) { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
			.ll .kicker { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
			.ll h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.9rem); line-height: 1.12; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
			.ll h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.2; }
			.ll .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; }
			.ll .toc { max-width: 44rem; margin: 1.25rem auto 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
			.ll .toc li { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
			.ll code { background: var(--ll-panel-2); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
			.ll .act { margin: 3.5rem 0; scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
			.ll .hero-act { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ll-accent) 5%, transparent); border-radius: 18px; padding: 2rem 0.5rem; }
			.ll .act-tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; background: var(--ll-accent); padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
			.ll .act-tag.star { background: var(--ll-loyal); }
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .ll .act-tag { color: #0e1114; } }
			.ll .point { font-size: 1.05rem; }
			.ll .aside { max-width: 44rem; margin: 1.25rem auto 0; font-size: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--ll-accent); padding-left: 0.9rem; }
			.ll .fineprint { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); }
			.ll .links a { display: inline-block; margin-right: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; }

			.ll .panel { max-width: 52rem; margin: 1.5rem auto; background: var(--ll-panel); border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.25rem; }
			.ll .panel-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
			.ll .mini { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }

			.ll .chips { display: flex; gap: 0.45rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
			.ll .chip { padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); background: var(--ll-panel-2); color: var(--ll-ink); font: inherit; font-size: 0.85rem; cursor: pointer; }
			.ll .chip:hover { border-color: var(--ll-accent); }
			.ll .chip.on { background: var(--ll-accent); color: #fff; border-color: var(--ll-accent); }
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .ll .chip.on { color: #0e1114; } }

			.ll .textarea { width: 100%; padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); background: var(--ll-panel-2); color: var(--ll-ink); font: inherit; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; resize: vertical; white-space: pre-wrap; }
			.ll .row.controls { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0.75rem 0; }
			.ll .run-note { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); }
			.ll .dots { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; margin: 0.1rem 0 0.25rem; }
			.ll .dot { width: 0.5rem; height: 0.5rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ll-line); transition: background 0.2s, transform 0.2s; }
			.ll .dot.on { background: var(--ll-accent); transform: scale(1.25); }
			.ll .btn { padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); background: var(--ll-panel-2); color: var(--ll-ink); font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
			.ll .btn:hover { border-color: var(--ll-accent); }
			.ll .btn.primary { background: var(--ll-accent); color: #fff; border-color: var(--ll-accent); }
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .ll .btn.primary { color: #0e1114; } }

			.ll .brief-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; }
			.ll .brief-table th, .ll .brief-table td { padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ll-line); }
			.ll .brief-table th:first-child, .ll .brief-table td.c-name { text-align: left; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); }
			.ll .brief-table .firm { font-weight: 700; }
			.ll .brief-table .firm-p { color: var(--ll-loyal); }
			.ll .brief-table .c-win { color: var(--ll-ok); font-weight: 700; }
			.ll .brief-verdict { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
			.ll .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.9rem; }
			@media (max-width: 640px) { .ll .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
			.ll .model-card { border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 0.85rem; background: var(--ll-panel-2); }
			.ll .model-card.biased { border-left: 4px solid var(--ll-loyal); }
			.ll .model-card.twin { border-left: 4px solid var(--ll-twin); }
			.ll .model-head { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
			.ll .tag-bad, .ll .tag-neutral { font-size: 0.66rem; padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 999px; }
			.ll .tag-bad { background: var(--ll-bad-bg); color: var(--ll-bad); }
			.ll .tag-neutral { background: var(--ll-panel); color: var(--ll-ink-soft); border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); }
			.ll .choice { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; }
			.ll .pick { display: inline-block; min-width: 1.4em; text-align: center; padding: 0 0.35em; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--ll-accent); color: #fff; }
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .ll .pick { color: #0e1114; } }
			.ll .choice-note { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0.35rem 0; }
			.ll .flag-bad { color: var(--ll-bad); font-weight: 600; }
			.ll .flag-ok { color: var(--ll-twin); font-weight: 600; }
			.ll .rationale { font-size: 0.88rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin-top: 0.5rem; }

			/* lens */
			.ll .lens-panel { max-width: 52rem; }
			.ll .lens-controls { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
			.ll .toggle { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); border-radius: 999px; overflow: hidden; }
			.ll .tg { padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; border: none; background: var(--ll-panel-2); color: var(--ll-ink-soft); font: inherit; font-size: 0.85rem; cursor: pointer; }
			.ll .tg.on { background: var(--ll-accent); color: #fff; }
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .ll .tg.on { color: #0e1114; } }
			.ll .chart { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; overflow: visible; }
			.ll .layer-slider { width: calc(100% - 62px); margin: 0.25rem 0 0 46px; accent-color: var(--ll-accent); }
			.ll .layer-axis { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin: 0.1rem 0 0.5rem 46px; padding-right: 16px; }
			.ll .readouts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.6rem 1.2rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
			@media (max-width: 560px) { .ll .readouts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
			.ll .ro { border-top: 1px solid var(--ll-line); padding-top: 0.5rem; }
			.ll .ro.span { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
			.ll .ro-l { font-size: 0.85rem; }
			.ll .ro-sub { color: var(--ll-ink-soft); font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.78rem; }
			.ll .ro-v { font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
			.ll .ro-v.hot { color: var(--ll-loyal); }
			.ll .ro-v.flat { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); }
			.ll .ro-v .ro-sub { font-size: 0.75rem; }
			.ll .meter { height: 7px; background: var(--ll-panel-2); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.3rem; overflow: hidden; }
			.ll .meter-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 4px; transition: width 0.08s linear; }
			.ll .meter-fill.hot { background: var(--ll-loyal); }
			.ll .meter-fill.cool { background: var(--ll-dormant); }
			.ll .lens-narrate { font-size: 0.98rem; margin-top: 1rem; padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem; background: var(--ll-panel-2); border-radius: 8px; border-left: 3px solid var(--ll-accent); }
			.ll .caption { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ll-ink-soft); margin-top: 0.6rem; }

			.ll .tech { max-width: 44rem; margin: 1.25rem auto 0; border: 1px solid var(--ll-line); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--ll-panel); }
			.ll .tech summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ll-accent); }
			.ll .tech[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ll-line); }
			.ll .tech p { padding: 0 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
			.ll .tech p:last-child { padding-bottom: 1rem; }
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
